{"tool_name":"fluff","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"fluff","home":"https://github.com/simonvh/fluff","license":"MIT","summary":"fluff is a software package that allows for simple exploration, clustering and visualization of high-throughput sequencing data mapped to a reference genome.","addition_date":"2018-10-31T18:25:39Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T17:17:14Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:fluff","credit":[{"email":"s.vanheeringen@science.ru.nl","name":"Simon J. van Heeringen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0411-3219","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://fluff.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}]}],"name":"fluff","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/peerj.2209","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 Georgiou and Van Heeringen.Summary. In this article we describe fluff, a software package that allows for simple exploration, clustering and visualization of high-throughput sequencing data mapped to a reference genome. The package contains three command-line tools to generate publication-quality figures in an uncomplicated manner using sensible defaults. Genome-wide data can be aggregated, clustered and visualized in a heatmap, according to different clustering methods. This includes a predefined setting to identify dynamic clusters between different conditions or developmental stages. Alternatively, clustered data can be visualized in a bandplot. Finally, fluffincludes a tool to generate genomic profiles. As command-line tools, the fluffprograms can easily be integrated into standard analysis pipelines. The installation is straightforward and documentation is available at http://fluff.readthedocs.org. Availability. fluffis implemented in Python and runs on Linux. The source code is freely available for download at https://github.com/simonvh/fluff.","authors":[{"name":"Georgiou G."},{"name":"van Heeringen S.J."}],"citationCount":24,"date":"2016-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PeerJ","title":"Fluff: Exploratory analysis and visualization of high-throughput sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC4957989","pmid":"27547532","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Comparative genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0797"},{"term":"RNA-seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"fluff","home":"https://bio.tools/fluff","license":"MIT","summary":"fluff is a software package that allows for simple exploration, clustering and visualization of high-throughput sequencing data mapped to a reference genome.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:fluff/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":32,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2018"},{"count":4,"year":"2022"},{"count":5,"year":"2023"},{"count":6,"year":"2019"},{"count":6,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.7717/peerj.2209","pmcid":"PMC4957989","pmid":"27547532","ref_count":33,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":2,"year":"